   "_dt": 1793014622.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "The chief of Korean defense company LIG Defense & Aerospace Co. (LIG D&A) on Monday denied the company's involvement in a bribery scandal linked to weapons procurement bids. Appearing as a witness before the National Assembly's defense committee, LIG D&A CEO Shin Ick-hyun said two company executives indicted on charges of bribing an official at the Defense Acquisition Program Administration (DAPA) during weapons procurement tenders have maintained their innocence.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国国防企业LIG Defense & Aerospace Co.（LIG D&A）负责人周一否认公司卷入与武器采购投标有关的受贿丑闻。LIG D&A首席执行官申益铉出席国会国防委员会作证时表示，两名被控在武器采购招标期间向国防事业厅（DAPA）官员行贿、现已遭起诉的公司高管始终坚称自己无罪。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The chief of Korean defense company LIG Defense & Aerospace Co. (LIG D&A) on Monday denied the company's involvement in a bribery scandal linked to weapons procurement bids. Appearing as a witness before the National Assembly's defense committee, LIG D&A CEO Shin Ick-hyun said two company executives indicted on charges of bribing an official at the Defense Acquisition Program Administration (DAPA) during weapons procurement tenders have maintained their innocence. Last week, DAPA barred LIG D&A from bidding on defense contracts for two years over the bribery allegations, a move that could hamper the company's efforts to secure new domestic defense orders. LIG D&A expressed regret over the decision, arguing that the penalty was imposed before the criminal trial had concluded. The company said it plans to take legal action to challenge the ban. Shin acknowledged his moral responsibility as CEO for the incident but maintained that the company itself was not involved. He said LIG D&A has taken steps to reinforce its corporate compliance framework, including the establishment of a new compliance audit office",
