   "published": "Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:19:21 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793013561.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Davido’s aide, Damilare Aladegbola, popularly known as Dre, has appealed to the person who allegedly stole his phone during rapper Zlatan Ibile and Davita Lamai’s wedding ceremony to return it. The aide took to his Instagram on Monday, promising to reward whoever took the phone with money in exchange for its return. “If na u carry my phone for Zlatan wedding, abeg return am, I go give you money please,” he wrote in pidgin English.",
   "summary_zh": "达维多的一名助理达米拉雷·阿拉德格博拉（俗称Dre）已呼吁一名据称在歌手兹拉坦·伊比莱和达维塔·拉马伊婚礼期间偷走他手机的人归还手机。这名助理周一在Instagram上发文承诺，无论谁拿走了这部手机，只要归还，就会获得金钱作为回报。他用尼日利亚皮钦英语写道：“如果是你在兹拉坦的婚礼上拿走了我的手机，拜托归还，我会给你钱。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Davido’s aide, Damilare Aladegbola, popularly known as Dre, has appealed to the person who allegedly stole his phone during rapper Zlatan Ibile and Davita Lamai’s wedding ceremony to return it. The aide took to his Instagram on Monday, promising to reward whoever took the phone with money in exchange for its return. “If na u carry my phone for Zlatan wedding, abeg return am, I go give you money please,” he wrote in pidgin English. He further said, “From now on, if I go any party or dey any party and any stupid waitress tell me say are you done eating so I can pack your plate, na swear I go swear for you cause na pattern. Wey una dey use pack phone for table be that now.” PUNCH Online reports that Zlatan ties the knot with his longtime partner, Davita. Davido, K1, others grace Zlatan’s traditional wedding Evening recap: Shoprite plans comeback, Tinubu-Atiku clash over hunger, other stories PHOTOS: Zlatan, Davita shine in regal attire for traditional wedding The music star posted the wedding pictures on his official Instagram page ahead of their traditional wedding ceremony, which is being held on Saturday. He wrote, “IT’s TIME TO MARRY” Celebrities, fans, and well-wishers were at the wedding ceremony in Lagos, with Davido leading the pack of groomsmen at the event. Adekunle Sulaimon Adekunle, a fellow of Data and Solutions Journalism, has over four years experience with competences in data journalism and investigations",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
