   "title": "Anambra govt seeks NMA support in fight against illegal health facilities",
   "url": "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/regional/ssouth-east/920322-anambra-govt-seeks-nma-support-in-fight-against-illegal-health-facilities.html",
   "domain": "premiumtimesng.com",
   "source": "Premium Times（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:02:11 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793012531.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "The Anambra State Government has called on the Nigeria Medical Association (NMA) to support its efforts to eradicate quack and unregistered health facilities in the state. Adam Obidike, the commissioner for health in Anambra made the appeal during the closing ceremony of the 2026 Physicians Week and Scientific Conference of the Nigerian Medical Association, Awka Zone in Awka on Sunday.",
   "summary_zh": "阿南布拉州政府已呼吁尼日利亚医学协会支持该州根除非法行医场所和未注册医疗机构的努力。阿南布拉州卫生专员亚当·奥比迪克于周日在奥卡举行的尼日利亚医学协会奥卡区分会2026年医师周暨科学会议闭幕式上发出这一呼吁。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Anambra State Government has called on the Nigeria Medical Association (NMA) to support its efforts to eradicate quack and unregistered health facilities in the state. Adam Obidike, the commissioner for health in Anambra made the appeal during the closing ceremony of the 2026 Physicians Week and Scientific Conference of the Nigerian Medical Association, Awka Zone in Awka on Sunday. The theme of the Week, Luncheon and Award Presentation Ceremony was “Securing the Future of Medicine in Nigeria and Sub-Saharan Africa”. Mr Obidike, a medical doctor, said the NMA was a critical partner and that the government would collaborate with the association to track fake and unregistered facilities. “We are determined to shut all of them down because when people go there, they receive treatment that is not proper for their ailment. “We have a checklist and anybody who wants to set up a facility should go to the department of medical services and get the conditions, including the design of the building,” he said. In his welcome address, Tim-Uzoma Mbaeri, chairman of NMA, Awka Zone, said this year’s Physicians Week and Scientific Conference was a time to celebrate the profession and reconnect members with each other. Mr Mbaeri, a professor, said the association used the event to visit sick colleagues, provide free laboratory tests including prostate specific antigens testing, urinalysis among others. He thanked members and partners of the NMA, Awka branch, whose contributions ensured the success of the physicians’ week. “We also enjoyed a novelty football match, had an opportunity for friendship, recreation, and strong inter-agency relationships. “We find satisfaction not merely in the event we organised, but in the lives we have touched, the colleagues we have encouraged, the relationships we have strengthened and the visibility we have given to our profession,” he said. Mr Mbaeri said three personalities were honoured with awards of meritorious service to the medical profession and the NMA, including Ifeoma Njelita, Emmanuel Umenweke and Amaka Ezeno. Njelita is an associate professor and a consultant in community medicine at the Chukwuemeka Odumegwu Ojukwu University Teaching Hospital. Umenweke is a medical doctor with the Nnamdi Azikiwe University Medical Center, Awka while Ezeno, the third awardee is a lawyer, Notary Public and member of the Body of Benchers",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_premiumtimes",
   "title_zh": "安ambra州政府寻求尼日利亚医学会支持打击非法医疗机构",
   "body_zh": "阿纳姆拉州政府已呼吁尼日利亚医学协会支持该州打击、取缔虚假及未注册医疗机构的努力。阿纳姆拉州卫生专员亚当·奥比迪克于周日在奥沃卡举行的尼日利亚医学协会奥沃卡区分会2026年医师周暨科学会议闭幕式上提出这一呼吁。本届医师周、午餐会及颁奖典礼的主题是“保障尼日利亚和撒哈拉以南非洲医学的未来”。身为医学博士的奥比迪克先生表示，尼日利亚医学协会是重要的合作伙伴，政府将与该协会合作，追踪虚假和未注册的医疗机构。他说：“我们决心关闭所有这类机构，因为人们前往那里接受的治疗并不适合其疾病。我们有一份清单，任何想设立医疗机构的人都应前往医疗服务部门了解相关条件，包括建筑设计方案。”尼日利亚医学协会奥沃卡区分会主席蒂姆·乌佐马·姆巴埃里在欢迎辞中表示，今年的医师周暨科学会议是庆祝医学职业、让会员彼此重新联络交流的时刻。姆巴埃里教授说，该协会利用这次活动探望患病同事，并提供免费实验室检测，包括前列腺特异性抗原检测、尿液分析等。他感谢尼日利亚医学协会奥沃卡分会的会员和合作伙伴，正是他们的贡献确保了医师周圆满成功。他说：“我们还举办了一场别开生面的足球赛，获得了交流友谊、放松娱乐和加强机构间关系的机会。我们不仅从自己组织的活动中获得满足，也从帮助他人、鼓励同事、加强联系以及提升本职业社会可见度中感受到价值。”姆巴埃里先生表示，3人因对医学职业和尼日利亚医学协会作出卓越贡献而获颁奖项，包括伊费奥马·恩杰利塔、埃马纽埃尔·乌门韦克和阿玛卡·埃泽诺。恩杰利塔是楚库韦梅卡·奥杜梅格武·奥朱克武大学教学医院的社区医学副教授及顾问医师。乌门韦克是奥沃卡南纳姆迪·阿齐基韦大学医学中心的医学博士，第三位获奖者埃泽诺则是律师、公证人及律师公会成员。",
